    "reasoning": "All three earlier selections agree with the current captured worked solutions. For q-20512, R₂−2R₁ gives (0,1,0|4), and R₃−3R₁ gives (0,0,−2|8). Thus y=4, z=−4, and back substitution gives x=5. For q-8856, the coefficient matrix has determinant 40 and inverse (1/40)[6,−8;5,0]; multiplying by (6,7) gives the solution (−1/2,3/4). For q-102807, rewriting gives −x+2y=3 and x−y=−7. The inverse coefficient matrix is [1,2;1,1], whose product with (3,−7) gives (−11,−4). Both pairs satisfy their original equations. In the last two questions, the source writes x for the entire solution vector while also using x as a scalar coordinate; the selected expressions are correct under the intended vector notation. Confirmation is supported by each question's own worked solution; no grade evidence was supplied.",
